# Docs (Puck-style, one topic per page) & Testing

## Documentation

- Every public subsystem has its own doc page under `docs/page-builder/`
  (`concepts/`, `editor/`, `api/`, `guides/`) — one concern per file, like
  Puck's Config/Data/Fields/Render split. Never dump multiple subsystems
  into one README-style page.
- Each doc page states: the contract (inputs/outputs/invariants/failure
  modes), how a host extends it without forking, and its limits (payload
  size, nesting depth, locale fallback, etc.) and what happens when
  exceeded.
- **No silent drift**: if a code change alters a subsystem's contract, the
  matching doc page updates IN THE SAME PR/commit set. If you change
  behavior in `visibilityResolve.ts` but don't touch
  `docs/page-builder/concepts/visibility.md`, the change isn't complete.
- New `kind` values in the Model B field-adapter enum, new locale storage
  strategies, new visibility predicate keys, etc. — all require the doc
  update in the same change, not "as a follow-up."

## Testing — required coverage per area (§14)

When you touch code in a given subsystem, make sure the matching test
category exists and passes:

| Area touched | Required test |
|---|---|
| Any block | Smoke test: `render` + `ContentFields` + `propsSchema` |
| Registry | Drift test: required `BlockDefinition` fields present |
| Canvas / preview / Open Page | Same fixture renders comparable DOM across all three |
| CSS composer | Malformed CSS, `@import`, escape-selector rejection |
| CSS composer | Remote `url()` / `data:` exfiltration rejection |
| Sandbox policy | Exact `sandbox` string asserted; no `allow-same-origin`; CSP regression |
| canvasBridge | Wrong-origin / malformed-schema messages rejected |
| Rich text | Script / event-handler HTML stripped by sanitizer; Unicode preserved |
| Clipboard | Paste regenerates all ids; deep trees; history integration |
| Outline | Mirrors nested blocks; selection sync; hidden nodes still listed, dimmed |
| Preset expand | Inserts expected primitive tree |
| Locale resolve | en/ne (+extra) fallback; missing key → fallbackLocale; Unicode round-trip; flat-key normalization both directions |
| Preview | Large fixture opens via draft id/store key; URL length stays bounded |
| Visibility | `visibleWhen` + `visibility` evaluate identically across canvas/preview/Open Page; hidden blocks retain full tree data |
| Registration | Duplicate type errors; namespace enforcement; no eval path exists |
| Unknown block | Fallback UI renders; page doesn't crash; tree preserved |
| Repeater binding | Template expands once per item; empty/loading/error parity; token resolution doesn't emit unescaped HTML |
| Cross-strategy binding | Strategy A (host-resolved) and B (client fetch) produce identical DOM for one fixture DataSource |
| Item-scoped visibility | `item.*` predicates only resolve inside repeater scope; fail safe outside it |
| CSP nonce | No `'unsafe-inline'` in `script-src`/`style-src`; nonce mismatch rejected (capture via CSP violation report) |
| Accessibility | Core primitives + editor chrome pass WCAG 2.2 AA smoke checks (keyboard, labels, focus, contrast) |

If a change doesn't have a corresponding test from this table and it's not
obviously covered by an existing one, add it before considering the task
done — don't defer test-writing to "later."
